# VideosRipper agent workflow

## Commit tool changes

When you update VideosRipper (code under `videosripper/`, `scripts/`, `tests/`, `Makefile`, `configs/`, `LLM-RIP-WORKFLOW.md`, or other tracked repo files), **commit to git as part of the workflow**. Do not leave substantial tool changes uncommitted unless the user explicitly says not to commit.

Before committing:

1. Run from git root: `/mnt/game1/VideosRipper` (not `/home/lee/VideosRipper`).
2. Stage only repo/tool files — never runtime artifacts or secrets.
3. Use caveman-commit / Conventional Commits: `<type>(<scope>): <imperative summary>`, ≤50 chars when possible.

## Never commit

- `.venv/`, `output/`, `logs/`, ripped `*.mkv`, `.tmp/`
- Staging workflow artifacts under `staging/` (pending/ready/done/failed job files)
- Secrets: `.env`, `.env.*`, `*credentials*`, API keys

## Multi-disc movies

- One manifest per disc; output name: `Title (Year) - Disc N.mkv`
- When stitching parts: set `post.copy_to_nas: false` on each disc manifest
- Rip discs independently; stitch with `scripts/stitch-movie-parts.sh`
- Copy **only the stitched file** to NAS after join — not per-disc masters
